              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court held that the 2017 Act\u2019s quarterly fee increase violated the Bankruptcy Clause\u2019s uniformity requirement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "775a8ddc68188e880d9592028b515d07bfe207f528fb350a5874477ec3e08c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-775a8ddc6818-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court reversed the Fourth Circuit\u2019s judgment and remanded the case for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "775a8ddc68188e880d9592028b515d07bfe207f528fb350a5874477ec3e08c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-775a8ddc6818-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The fee increase was applied differently across regions; debtors in Alabama and North Carolina paid no increase for the first three quarters of 2018, while debtors elsewhere did."
      }
    ],
