                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Daniel L. Geyser, the petitioner argued that Congress arbitrarily divided the country into two groups and imposed different fees on identically situated debtors, violating the uniformity requirement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d43168ea462a3a142b9fb28e1a3be537a6e08ce881fe6ef12ab3dfe3fa40feba",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d43168ea462a-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 45,
                "start": 45
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Geyser, the petitioner asked the Court to equalize treatment by allowing debtors in the lower\u2011fee districts to pay the lower fees."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d43168ea462a3a142b9fb28e1a3be537a6e08ce881fe6ef12ab3dfe3fa40feba",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d43168ea462a-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Geyser, the petitioner indicated that the lower courts could be tasked with determining the appropriate remedy on remand."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner\u2019s Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
